= Natural history
{parent=Biology}
{wiki}

Study of <organisms> and other natural objects through observation, collection and description; historically it included subjects now separated among several sciences.

= Linnean Society
{parent=Natural history}
{c}
{wiki=Linnean_Society_of_London}

The learned society to which materials by <Charles Darwin> and <Alfred Russel Wallace> were communicated together on 1 July 1858.

= Naturalist
{parent=Natural history}

A practitioner who observes, collects, describes or classifies <organisms> and other natural objects. The historical role predates modern disciplinary divisions among <biology>, <geology> and related subjects.

= List of naturalists
{parent=Naturalist}

