{parent=Medicine}

Treatment intended to increase urine output. Current guidance uses monitored <diuretic therapy> for <acute heart failure>; it is distinct from loss of <blood> through <venesection>. <Acute heart failure by NICE>[CG187 §§1.3.3–1.3.5]{ref}

= Enema
{parent=Medicine}

Introduction of fluid into the lower <intestine>. A selected case of <faecal impaction> is a possible modern indication; this does not support routine evacuation in a weak febrile patient. <Constipation by the NHS>[Complications of long-term constipation]{ref}

