= Cardiac rupture
{parent=Cardiology}

A breach in a wall of the <heart>. Free-wall rupture can allow <blood> to enter the <pericardium>, causing <haemopericardium> and potentially <cardiac tamponade>. <Mechanical Complications of Acute Myocardial Infarction by the American Heart Association>[Free wall rupture]{ref}

= Valvulitis
{parent=Cardiology}

Inflammation of a cardiac valve.

= Sinus rhythm
{parent=Cardiology}

= Heart sound
