= Pericarditis
{parent=Cardiology}

<Inflammation> of the <pericardium>; its cause and haemodynamic complications determine management.

= Pericardial friction rub
{parent=Pericarditis}

An auscultatory sign produced by movement of inflamed pericardial surfaces.

= Pericardial effusion
{parent=Pericarditis}

Accumulation of fluid in the <pericardium>. Its size and effect on the circulation are distinct questions.

= Haemopericardium
{parent=Pericardial effusion}

= Hemopericardium
{synonym}

<Blood> within the <pericardium>; a sufficiently rapid collection can cause <cardiac tamponade>. <Mechanical Complications of Acute Myocardial Infarction by the American Heart Association>[Free wall rupture]{ref}

