A follicular disorder with keratotic papules and scaling plaques; distinct from the broad historical label <pityriasis rubra>.

= Seborrhoeic dermatitis
{parent=Dermatology}

= Dandruff
{parent=Dermatology}

Fine scalp scaling, commonly the relatively uninflamed scalp form of <seborrhoeic dermatitis>.

= Desquamation
{parent=Dermatology}

Shedding of the surface layers of the <epidermis>.

= Pityriasis
{parent=Dermatology}

A historical descriptive group of <skin> disorders with fine bran-like <desquamation>. Its former varieties do not constitute one modern disease.

= Pityriasis nigra
{parent=Pityriasis}

An unstable historical category for dark eruptions or pigmentation, sometimes described as dark <pityriasis versicolor>. It cannot be assigned one modern pathogen from the name alone.

= Pityriasis rubra
{parent=Pityriasis}

Historical name for a red, scaling eruption. It is not automatically equivalent to <pityriasis rubra pilaris>.

= Pityriasis capitis
{parent=Pityriasis}

Historical description of fine scalp scaling; many cases correspond to <dandruff>. The name alone does not establish a cause.

